# Instrument Form Beauty Grammar

**CRITICAL:** Sealed optical/electronic instruments must look **inevitable and well-designed** — form forced by function, hand/eye, materials, and manufacturing — never by pasting a gold product silhouette.

Hand/eye floors live in `human-factors-instrument-form.mdc` (Apple HIG). This rule is the rest of the stack.

## The stack (encode all of these)

```
optics / sample / power / HMI / service
  → volumes + joints          (use-physics)
  → mm floors for eye/hand    (Apple HIG via human_factors_instrument)
  → materials per role        (honesty table)
  → control taxonomy          (Fitts)
  → dress + fasteners         (loom + AM language)
  → structured interior       (optical bench composition)
  → SIGHT proveCatch          (vision / geometry guards)
```

Gold open-photometer photos are the **TRAINING check**, not a paste target.

## 1. Use-physics → exterior features

| Function | Forced form |
|---|---|
| Light-tight optical path | Chunky near-cubic chamber (not a chimney) |
| Top-loading cuvette | Square well + circular rim for ambient-light cap |
| Beer–Lambert I₀ | Cap exists; parks on UI deck in product hero (well stays readable) |
| Wavelength swap | Source PCB on optical-axis face + cable channel at cube↔body joint |
| Operate looking down | Recessed dark glass + controls on the **top** deck |
| AM enclosure | Visible top-plate fasteners on a quiet grid |

## 2. Material honesty

| Role | Material language | Forbidden |
|---|---|---|
| Body / cube | Charcoal matte polymer | Appliance light-grey slabs |
| Display | Dark glass (LCD at rest) + subtle bezel | Green FR4 under glass on closed hero; pale “patch” as screen |
| Keys | Hard dark tactile keys (prefer **square**) | 2–3 mm cosmetic pegs / rivets |
| Source / compute boards | Green FR4 + gold pads | FR4 painted as the exterior screen |
| Screws | Dark metallic heads that read at product scale | Invisible or missing fasteners |

Constants: `scripts/lib/instrument_form_grammar.py`.

## 3. Fitts + control taxonomy

- **D-pad** left of glass (navigate)
- **A/B** right of glass (commit)
- Pitch ≥ finger gap from Apple floors
- Keys sized to HIG diameter (≥7 mm, prefer 9 mm), **square** plan when the grammar says square

## 4. Rams / quiet industrial design

- As few exterior features as the functions above require — no decorative vents, fake knobs, or sticker clutter
- Align display, keys, well, and screws to one top-deck grid
- One primary composition: buttons → glass → optical cube

## 5. Loom grammar

Connector on source board → strain-relief boot → multi-colour dressed loom → **molded cable channel** at the cube↔body joint → interior. Never mid-air stubs into a lid.

## 6. Interior cutaway (must be beautiful and structured)

The Excel “Interior — cutaway” view (`00-hero.png` for instruments) MUST show a **readable optical/electronics story**, not zone-stacked grey slabs:

```
LEFT (UI volume)          RIGHT (optical volume)
  coin cell + main PCB      source → beam → cuvette → detector
  under the display locus   aligned to the exterior cube / well axis
```

- One horizontal optical axis through the sample
- PCB and power live under the UI deck, not as a vertical BESS stack
- Interior anchors come from `_instrument_form_rule_mm` — exterior and interior share the same geometry truth
- Translucent shell is intentional; story colours must stay (equipment module, not `structure_containment`)

## 7. View contract

| View | Instrument meaning |
|---|---|
| `04` / `05` / `06` / `07` | Closed product exterior |
| `00-hero` | **Open cutaway** — structured interior (Excel “Interior — cutaway”) |

Do not close `00-hero` for instruments — that hides the interior and defeats the Excel label.

